GF_SdatGetAttrPtr(0/1) by sub_020055AC) in u32 slots, but a handle is a pointer (NNSSndWaveOutHandle): on the host the 8-byte
store of the primary handle overwrote the secondary slot, and the secondary's store the current-bank word at 0xBEBA4, so a
move sound that allocates both channels (Hyper Voice: the cry plays through the wave-out path) left the primary handle
half-clobbered and IsCryFinished -> sub_02005738 -> NNS_SndWaveOutIsPlaying read through it. Both slots are NNSSndWaveOutHandle
(4 bytes on the DS, the same layout). Drop when upstream types the two fields.
